{"w":2400,"lines":[{"y":0.064937471475998043,"t":"Audioscripts","x":0.12958892869543664,"c":1,"w":0.11112289428710939,"h":0.016927382597521023},{"c":1,"x":0.1296345293829998,"t":"hatched out of their eggs, they have hardly any contact with their parents. So, there's not","y":0.10886863772544442,"w":0.65615259806315107,"h":0.020777852782417061},{"w":0.03571428616841632,"t":"Q36","c":1,"x":0.82706766907744589,"h":0.013081395234588844,"y":0.11046511620538002},{"c":1,"y":0.12645348851498361,"w":0.30075187683105464,"x":0.12781954720477348,"t":"really any evidence to support that idea.","h":0.015988371407532731},{"t":"Another suggestion's based on the observation that male lizards in monogamous","w":0.59595952351888015,"x":0.13153084955813682,"h":0.015417844498456845,"y":0.14914516692008861,"c":1},{"h":0.014598526497157427,"y":0.16569767460967666,"c":1,"x":0.12781954501717185,"w":0.65789474487304689,"t":"relationships tend to be bigger and stronger than other males. So maybe the male lizards"},{"w":0.73322072347005207,"t":"stay around so they can give the female lizards protection from other males. But again, we're Q37","c":1,"h":0.018322453987038023,"x":0.12963932625995198,"y":0.17999855255966168},{"x":0.13105670457571791,"y":0.19580276922228701,"h":0.016582866061984891,"w":0.11195977528889972,"c":1,"t":"not really sure."},{"x":0.12962541052725896,"c":1,"y":0.21798268017995093,"w":0.68249450683593749,"h":0.019737780362808932,"t":"Finally, I'd like to mention another study that involved collecting data by tracking the lizards. I"},{"y":0.23535093347216129,"w":0.68609024047851563,"x":0.1296992406033535,"c":1,"t":"was actually involved in this myself. So we caught some lizards in the wild and we developed","h":0.014649066323245363},{"x":0.12969924726413259,"w":0.67293233235677075,"h":0.014539563264374,"t":"a tiny GPS system that would allow us to track them, and we fixed this onto their tails. Then","y":0.25144880862642194,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"we set the lizards free again, and we were able to track them for twelve days and gather data,","x":0.13157894976467921,"h":0.013081395234588844,"y":0.26744186052029384,"w":0.68796991984049483},{"x":0.12969925950048813,"c":1,"t":"not just about their location, but even about how many steps they took during this period.","y":0.28332260142873111,"w":0.65601501464843748,"h":0.014642514648240956},{"x":0.12969923736965816,"w":0.67105265299479167,"y":0.30521571166404415,"h":0.016097875080489321,"c":1,"t":"One surprising thing we discovered from this is that there were far fewer meetings between"},{"c":1,"h":0.017115494702910961,"t":"lizards than we expected - it seems that they were actually trying to avoid one another. So","x":0.1277811150390511,"y":0.32117434166362024,"w":0.66737945556640621},{"h":0.014810045074050149,"c":1,"t":"why would that be? Well, again we have no clear evidence, but one hypothesis is that male","y":0.33708950432562501,"x":0.12969924725874005,"w":0.67293233235677086},{"w":0.039473683039347285,"c":1,"h":0.013081395234588844,"t":"Q40","x":0.82330827117935335,"y":0.33720930234423085},{"x":0.12781954246843175,"c":1,"t":"lizards can cause quite serious injuries to one another, so maybe this avoidance is a way of","w":0.67669174194335935,"h":0.014545178459447583,"y":0.35318737947812828},{"t":"preventing this - of self-preservation, if you like. But we need to collect a lot more data before","c":1,"h":0.016097875080489321,"y":0.36767546697582265,"w":0.68796991984049471,"x":0.12969925048622183},{"t":"we can be sure of any of this.","y":0.38662790701206606,"c":1,"w":0.21804512023925779,"x":0.13157894369616055,"h":0.013081395234588844},{"w":0.035714286168416348,"h":0.013081395234588844,"c":1,"t":"112","x":0.12593984930300989,"y":0.94622093025120768}],"h":3106}